## Bus Factor: `src/Parser`

Period: all history. Today is 2026-10-22. The last commit in the repo is 2026-08-26, which is 57 days ago.

**Project-level bus factor for `src/Parser`: 2.** Graham Campbell and Aiko Tanaka together own about 90% of surviving lines. Losing Graham alone leaves about 55% of lines without a knowledgeable maintainer.

### Surviving code by author (`git blame -w -M -C`, 1,617 lines)

| Author | Lines | Share | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| Graham Campbell | 782 | 48% | `EntryParser`, `Value`, `Lines`, `Lexer`, `Parser`, `Entry`, `ParserInterface` |
| Aiko Tanaka (`Aiko Tanaka` plus `aiko tanaka`) | 637 | 39% | `Escape.php`, `Unicode/CharTable.php` |
| `root` | 117 | 7% | `Quirks.php` |
| `Your Name` | 69 | 4% | `Compat.php` |
| Vance Lucas, JT Smith, Jonas Staudenmeir, StyleCI Bot | 12 | under 1% | scattered lines |

The two Aiko spellings are probably one person with two git `user.name` settings. I did not check emails.

### Who to ask

- **`Lexer.php`: Graham Campbell.** Sole author with 7 commits and 100% of the 58 surviving lines. The last substantive change was 2020-06-07 ("Tweaked lexing", "Improved parsing performance"). His most recent commit on this file is 2026-08-24, a static-analysis cleanup.
- **Escape handling: Aiko Tanaka.**
  - `Escape.php` is 100% theirs: 2 commits, both on 2026-08-26 ("Add escape sequence handling", "Escape: more sequences").
  - `Unicode/CharTable.php` is also 100% theirs.
  - Both files are less than 2 months old. They are brand new compared with the Graham-owned core.

### Risks for the audit

- **Lexer and escapes have different owners.** `Lexer.php` has no `Escape` commits. Escape handling was added later as a separate file. Check how the two connect. Graham knows the lexing side and Aiko knows the escape side, and neither is the sole expert on the boundary. I did not read the code to confirm the call path.
- **Unattributed code.** `Quirks.php` (author `root`, commit message "fix") and `Compat.php` (author `Your Name`, "compat shims") have no identifiable human owner. Both were committed on 2026-08-26, the same day as the escape work, probably from a machine with no configured git identity. Ask Aiko first, since the timing matches. Treat both files as unreviewed. They are the highest-risk files in the module.
- **Dependents not checked.** I skipped the importer-count step, so I have no per-file criticality ranking. Every file is single-owner, so bus factor is 1 per file except `Entry.php` and `Lines.php`, which have 2 to 3 authors but one dominant owner.
- **Activity.** Graham (16 commits) and Aiko (3 commits) both committed within the last 90 days. Nobody on this module is inactive by that measure. All 90-day activity falls on 2026-08-24 to 2026-08-26, so "active" mostly reflects one burst of work.

### Suggested audit order

1. `Escape.php`, `Unicode/CharTable.php`, `Quirks.php`, `Compat.php`: new, concentrated, partly unattributed. Interview Aiko.
2. `Lexer.php` and its interface with `Escape.php`: interview Graham and Aiko together.
3. `EntryParser.php`: 362 lines, 22 commits, all Graham. It is the largest and most stable file.

