FINAL ANSWER:
Graham Campbell is the person to ask about `Lexer.php`. Aiko Tanaka is the person for escape handling. This is inferred from commit history, so it is a starting point.

**Who wrote `src/Parser`**
- **Graham Campbell** wrote almost all of it. He has about 430 commits across 5 emails, and his latest is 2026-08-24, so he is active. He is the sole author of `Lexer.php`, `Parser.php`, `EntryParser.php`, `Lines.php` and `Value.php`, apart from a few minor edits below.
- **Aiko Tanaka** wrote `Escape.php` (206 lines, 2 commits) and `Unicode/CharTable.php` (431 lines). All 3 commits are from 2026-08-26, in PR #1 (`feature/escapes`), which Graham merged. They appear under 3 spellings of the same name and email, differing only in case.
- Minor edits came from Jonas Staudenmeir (a PHP 8.4 commit in 2024), JT Smith (a typo fix in 2022) and Dan Heggø (a small edit in `Parser.php` and `EntryParser.php`). None of them is a useful contact.

**`Lexer.php`**
- Graham made all 7 commits, and `git blame` attributes all 58 lines to him. The last change was 2026-08-24, a static-analysis cleanup (#614).
- Ask him why it is built the way it is. The 2026-08-23 and 08-24 commits are the most relevant for an audit:
  - `8bf174e`: "Fix memory-safety crash on invalid UTF-8 variable names (#602)"
  - `dd5b391`: "Remove quadratic value parsing (#604)"
  - `4426075`: comments no longer start multiline values (#615)
  - `226b4ed`: diagnostics and messages (#607)

**Escape handling**
- `Escape.php` is entirely Aiko's, and Graham reviewed and merged it. Ask Aiko about the design and Graham about the review.
- This code is about two months old, and Aiko's only commits are that one-day burst. Confirm Aiko is still reachable before you rely on them. I can't tell from git.

**Risks for the audit**
- **Bus factor 1:** the tool flags `/src/Parser/` as bus factor 1, owned by Graham and Aiko. It reports no orphaned zones.
- **Code with no real author:**
  - `Quirks.php` (117 lines) was committed by `root <root@localhost>` with the message "fix".
  - `Compat.php` (69 lines) was committed by `Your Name <<email redacted>>` with the message "compat shims".
  - Both are from 2026-08-26, are the newest code in the directory, and have no contact. They look like commits made with a default git identity. Treat them as unreviewed and ask Graham where they came from.
- **Short history:** the repo has 616 commits going back years, so thin history is not a caveat here. Most of the recent security-relevant change landed in the last week of the history (2026-08-23 to 08-26), which is a reason to review it first.

I ran the ownership script with `--dry-run`, so nothing was written to the repo.

